{
  "dom_id": "step-e5231",
  "name": "Example: Calculating Binomial Coefficients Using the Formula",
  "problem": "Determine the value of $\\displaystyle{5 \\choose 4}.$",
  "worked_solution": "The binomial coefficient $\\displaystyle{n \\choose r}$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{n \\choose r} = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,  r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n = 5$ and $r = 4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{5}{4}) & =\\frac{5!}{(5-4)!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4!}{1!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{1\\cdot \\cancel{4!}} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
